    "['set policy-options policy-statement [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'isis 1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'isis 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper configuration command into Huawei equivalent:\\n\\nFor the Juniper command:\\n```\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0 passive\\n```\\n\\nThe Huawei equivalent is:\\n##\\nisis 1\\n silent-interface LoopBack0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `passive` is used to indicate that IS-IS should not send Hellos on the interface but still advertise it.\\n- In Huawei, the equivalent is `silent-interface` under the IS-IS process context.\\n- The LoopBack0 interface is assumed to be the equivalent of Juniper's lo0 interface.\", 'trans_template': 'isis 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'silent-interface LoopBack0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'silent-interface LoopBack0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper configuration command into Huawei equivalent:\\n\\nFor the Juniper command:\\n```\\nset protocols isis interface lo0.0 passive\\n```\\n\\nThe Huawei equivalent is:\\n##\\nisis 1\\n silent-interface LoopBack0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Juniper, `passive` is used to indicate that IS-IS should not send Hellos on the interface but still advertise it.\\n- In Huawei, the equivalent is `silent-interface` under the IS-IS process context.\\n- The LoopBack0 interface is assumed to be the equivalent of Juniper's lo0 interface.\", 'trans_template': 'silent-interface LoopBack0'}]]": 1,
