    "['set policy-options policy-statement [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'isis 1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'isis 1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper command `set protocols isis interface lo0.0 passive` to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\n##\\nisis 1\\n silent-interface LoopBack0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Huawei, IS-IS passive interfaces are configured using the `silent-interface` command under the IS-IS process\\n- The Juniper `passive` setting for IS-IS on loopback interfaces is equivalent to Huawei's `silent-interface` command\\n- The translation assumes IS-IS process number 1 (which is common default) and the standard loopback interface name (LoopBack0)\", 'trans_template': 'isis 1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'silent-interface LoopBack0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'silent-interface LoopBack0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper command `set protocols isis interface lo0.0 passive` to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\n##\\nisis 1\\n silent-interface LoopBack0\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- In Huawei, IS-IS passive interfaces are configured using the `silent-interface` command under the IS-IS process\\n- The Juniper `passive` setting for IS-IS on loopback interfaces is equivalent to Huawei's `silent-interface` command\\n- The translation assumes IS-IS process number 1 (which is common default) and the standard loopback interface name (LoopBack0)\", 'trans_template': 'silent-interface LoopBack0'}]]": 1,
